  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Este y ese",
    "@en": "This and that."
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**This** significa «este, esta, esto» (cerca) y **that**, «ese, esa, aquel, aquella» (lejos). En plural: **these** significa «estos, estas» y **those**, «esos, esas, aquellos, aquellas».",
     "@en": "**This** means «This, this, this.» (close) and **that**, «That, that, that, that» (away). In plural: **these** means «These, these.» and **those**, «those, those, those, those»."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**What's this?** — **It's a book**. En plural: **What are these?** — **They're books**. Para una **thing** (cosa) en singular se usa **it**; en plural, **they**.",
     "@en": "**What's this?** — **It's a book**. In plural: **What are these?**-**They're books**. For a **thing** (thing) in singular **it** is used; in plural, **they**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para preguntar por el color, di **What colour is this?** (¿De qué color es esto?).",
     "@en": "To ask about the color, say **What colour is this?** (What color is this?)."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "tabla",
