  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "El plural",
    "@en": "The plural"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "La mayoría de los sustantivos añaden **-s**: book → books, key → keys. Si acaban en -s, -x, -ch o -sh, suelen añadir **-es**: watch → watches.",
     "@en": "Most nouns add **-s**: book → books, key → keys. If they end up in -s, -x, -ch or -sh, they usually add **-es**: watch → watches."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Si acaban en consonante + **y**, cambia la **y** por **-ies**: family → families. Si hay vocal antes de la **y**, solo se añade **-s**: key → keys.",
     "@en": "If you end up in consonant + **y**, change the **y** to **-ies**: family → families. If there is a vowel before the **y**, only **-s**: key → keys are added."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Algunos plurales son irregulares: child → children. Los adjetivos no cambian: **a new book**, **two new books**. Son reglas frecuentes; hay excepciones.",
     "@en": "Some plurals are irregular: child → children. Adjectives do not change: **a new book**, **two new books**. They are common rules; there are exceptions."
    }
   ]
  },
